Package: lexio
Type: Package
Title: Generalized Input-Output Model with Preemptive Goal Programming
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Filipe Vasconcelos", family = "Rocha",
           email = "filipvasconcelos1@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0927-3799", affiliation = "PPGE/UFJF"))
Description: A generalized input-output model solved by preemptive
    (lexicographic) goal programming. The user declares an input-output
    database (technical structure, gross output, final demand, any number
    of satellite accounts and, optionally, a corridor that bounds the
    economic deviations on both sides, only below or only above) and the
    direction and goal of each account. Sectoral output is chosen to meet
    the goals in priority order, written as G x + d- - d+ = g. Each priority
    level is a linear program solved with GLPK, with the optima of the
    earlier levels locked; a level may hold several goals. By default all
    k! orders of the k satellite accounts are run, with the economic block
    fixed at the last level; the operator may list the orderings to run
    and, by an explicit declaration, move the economic block. The economic
    deviations can be absolute or relative to each goal. Every level of
    every run is reported, in tables and in an Excel workbook. The method
    follows Rocha (2026, doctoral thesis, Federal University of Juiz de
    Fora); the package includes the goal programming example of Miller and
    Blair (2022).
